{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795689769,"nonce":"MkNUglvdcvd+As11i0SC1drGQrY=","title":"AudioPlayer::seek blocks if the output device stops taking samples","message":"On desktop, seek calls rodio's Player::try_seek (0.22), which waits until the audio thread takes the order. If nothing pulls samples from the mixer, for example after the output device is lost, the call does not return. Read from rodio's source, not reproduced with a device.\n\nThe other case of this, a seek ordered in the last samples of a track, is handled: the player opens a track near its end again before it seeks, and a test covers it.\n\nA fix runs the order off the calling thread with a time limit, or needs rodio to drop an order that no source can take.\n\nLeft over from 8b9d523f5bbfa88e635218190f563246912fbd44770ff63f338d30942476dc36.","files":null}]}